            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0141" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg53"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Egan to Mr. Wharton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 315.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The present cabinet shows a very earnest
                    desire to cultivate good relations with the Government of the United States and
                    with this legation; and as I intimated in my telegram the minister of foreign
                        <pb facs="0142" n="54" xml:id="pg54"/> relations, Señor don Isidoro
                    Errazuriz, has expressed his strong desire to make with me a prompt and friendly
                    settlement of the <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi> claims, and has also
                    expressed his willingness to aid in every way in having the other claims
                    considered and finally disposed of. I would suggest that the claim of Patrick
                    Shields, of the steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Keeweenauw</hi>, should be dealt
                    with along with the <hi rendition="#italic">Baltimore</hi> claims, as I have
                    reason to know there is a good disposition to settle that at same time, provided
                    the compensation claimed be not unreasonable.</p>
                <p>The long delay that has taken place in relation to the claims arising out of the
                    war between Chile and Peru has entailed great hardships upon many of the
                    claimants, but especially in the cases of Mr. DuBois and some of those whose
                    homes were so wantonly destroyed after the battles of Miraflores and Chorillas.
                    Those claims should, I submit, be pressed to an early settlement.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Patrick Egan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
